      "grammar": "The finite verb sasarja governs the five accusative-plural descriptions ghorān, asurān, trīn, mahābalān, and uditān/sthitān. The final image is syntactically compressed: kālān is plural while mūrtim is singular. The translation therefore retains the sense of repeated embodiments of Kāla without pretending the line is ordinary prose.",
