      "source_label": "Yoga-Vāsiṣṭha 4.25.38",
      "devanagari": "कर्मजीवकलां तन्वीमसारां च मनोभिदाम् । अपुष्टां कृत्रिमामन्तश्चोदयोदयमागताः",
      "iast": "karmajīvakalāṃ tanvīmasārāṃ ca manobhidām | apuṣṭāṃ kṛtrimāmantaścodayodayamāgatāḥ",
      "english": "{9:They had come to} {8:the arising of an inward prompting}: {0:a portion of action-life}, {1:slender}, {2:without substance}, {3:and} {4:a division of mind}, {5:not yet nourished}, {6:constructed} {7:within}.",
      "grammar": "The accusative feminine sequence karma-jīva-kalām … mano-bhidām … apuṣṭām kṛtrimām is the object of āgatāḥ in the idiom udayam āgatāḥ, ‘came to arising.’ The exact internal relation of karma, jīva, and kalā is compact; ‘portion of action-life’ preserves the members rather than resolving them into a speculative psychology. kṛtrimām is the strongest individual support for ‘artificial,’ while the surrounding syntax supplies inward prompting rather than mechanical hardware.",
      "words": [
        {"i":0,"iast":"karma-jīva-kalām","deva":"कर्मजीवकलाम्","gloss":"a portion of action-life","parts":[{"form":"karman","gloss":"action; enacted operation"},{"form":"jīva","gloss":"living principle; life"},{"form":"kalā","gloss":"a small portion or functional part"}],"stem":"karma-jīva-kalā","root":"√kṛ (tanādi, 8U); √jīv (bhvādi, 1P)","rootGloss":"to do; to live","affix":"am (dvitīyā-ekavacana feminine)","morph":"accusative singular feminine compound","karaka":"object complement within udayam āgatāḥ","compound":{"type":"ṣaṣṭhī-tatpuruṣa, exact internal scope compact","vigraha":"karma-jīvasya kalā","members":["karman","jīva","kalā"]},"rootEvidence":{"kri":{"locus":"08.0010","aupadeshika_devanagari":"डुकृञ्","artha_sanskrit":"करणे"},"jiv":{"locus":"01.0643","aupadeshika_devanagari":"जीवँ","artha_sanskrit":"प्राणधारणे"}},"note":"The compound is kept close to its members; it is not expanded into an unevidenced theory of an individual soul."},
        {"i":1,"iast":"tanvīm","deva":"तन्वीम्","gloss":"slender; slight","parts":[{"form":"tanvī","gloss":"slender; slight"},{"form":"-m","gloss":"accusative singular"}],"stem":"tanvī","root":null,"affix":"am (dvitīyā-ekavacana)","morph":"accusative singular feminine","karaka":"qualifies kalām/bhidām"},
        {"i":2,"iast":"asārām","deva":"असाराम्","gloss":"without substance; insubstantial","parts":[{"form":"a-","gloss":"not; without"},{"form":"sāra","gloss":"substance; firmness"},{"form":"-ām","gloss":"accusative singular feminine"}],"stem":"asāra","root":null,"affix":"am (dvitīyā-ekavacana feminine)","morph":"accusative singular feminine","karaka":"qualifies kalām/bhidām","compound":{"type":"nañ-tatpuruṣa","vigraha":"na sāraḥ yasyāḥ sā","members":["a-","sāra"]}},
